alPjFsp7OMqLhlog87ykzCrElxBOdgoLurmrfhQgvL7fI1jx_iuxYT6QNhiVbP7CPtNSHBekziOT4vMdY0Yf3hM0zBXH3Yx-5aE6tBxh6UdxWS2ACnm8weR0S-U\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering file requirements**\\n\\nI need to use the kidney-pipeline-execution skill, but first, I should read about it. I might need to ask the user for the file, since it seems there might be an attachment missing from their prompt. I'll want to inspect any message attachments, but none were provided. It's possible there is an uploaded file in the workspace, so I need to mention that. I'll read the skill before replying, as it clearly applies to this task.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_uVWUA53hpqqEz8OpVAK1llBA|fc_0e33da8a38a28db00169bdb2fa87148191b1c3d7a920584241","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":391,"output":115,"cacheRead":8448,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8954,"cost":{"input":0.0009775,"output":0.001725,"cacheRead":0.0021119999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.004814499999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774039794488}}
{"type":"message","id":"8ec8f159","parentId":"f1201a7b","timestamp":"2026-03-20T20:50:02.689Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_uVWUA53hpqqEz8OpVAK1llBA|fc_0e33da8a38a28db00169bdb2fa87148191b1c3d7a920584241","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: kidney-pipeline-execution\ndescription: Execute the kidney cancer CT pipeline by uploading a user-provided kidney CT image, taking the real uploaded image path returned by the upload endpoint, replacing the image-path placeholder inside the fixed prototype request JSON, then sending that request to the kidney pipeline execution endpoint and summarizing the Kidney Cancer Detector, Image Analyzer, and X-AI outputs. Use when a user wants to run the integrated kidney pipeline on a CT scan image and inspect either the raw response or a clean summary of the main outputs.\n---\n\n# Kidney Pipeline Execution\n\nUpload the user image first, use the returned upload path in the fixed request template, then execute the kidney pipeline.\n\n## Required behavior\n\nFollow this sequence exactly:\n\n1. Determine the local CT image to analyze.\n   - Prefer the explicit user-provided local image path.\n   - If no path is provided, use the newest supported image under `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n2. Require the Telegram user id.\n   - Pass it as `--telegram-user-id` or set `TELEGRAM_USER_ID`.\n   - Use that value as the upload request's `user_id` query parameter.\n3. Upload the image with `POST multipart/form-data` to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=<telegram-user-id>`\n4. Read the upload response JSON.\n   - Build the real remote image path as `path + filename`.\n   - Use the returned path from the upload response only.\n   - Do not keep example paths, stale upload paths, or unresolved placeholders in the executed request.\n5. Load `references/request-template.json`.\n6. Replace every <image-path-here> placeholder in the template with the real uploaded image path (rows 56, 208, 305, 371, 396).\n7. Send the resulting JSON payload to:\n   - `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n8. Read the pipeline response and summarize it by module:\n   - Kidney Cancer Detector\n   - Image Analyzer\n   - X-AI\n9. If the analyzer image URL exists at `response.workflows[0].branches[0].nodes[0].children[0].children[0].tracking.parameters.file_path`, extract the URL and include the image in the normal reply.\n10. Do not send out-of-band Telegram messages from the script.\n\n## Fixed values\n\nKeep these values fixed:\n- `storage_ref`: `nodes_bucket`\n- `local_file_path`: `upload/`\n- execution endpoint: `http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/prototype_execution/prototype_execution/`\n- request template: `references/request-template.json`\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- Treat the request template as a fixed prototype payload, but always inject the freshly uploaded image path before execution.\n- Fail loudly if `<image_path_here>` remains anywhere in the payload after replacement.\n- If template fields such as `filename`, `pdf_path`, or `File Path` contain placeholder or stale upload-path values, replace them with the fresh uploaded image path before execution.\n- Preserve the response wrapper shape returned by the script.\n- If the endpoint returns non-JSON text, return that text as the `response` value.\n\n## Preferred script\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id <telegram-user-id> [local-image-path]\n```\n\nIf `local-image-path` is omitted, the script should select the newest supported image from `/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound`.\n\n## Summary fields to prioritize\n\nWhen present, summarize these fields first.\n\n### Kidney Cancer Detector\n- `Inference time`\n- `classes`\n- `confidence`\n\n### Image Analyzer\n- `cam_metrics`\n- `prediction`\n- `cam_explanation`\n- `file_path` when useful for returning the analyzer image\n\nWhen `cam_metrics` is present, include all available subfields such as:\n- `coverage`\n- `center_ratio`\n- `lr_asym`\n- `tb_asym`\n\n### X-AI\n- `confidence_interpretation`\n- `recommended_next_steps`\n- `references`\n- `summary`\n- `visual_evidence`\n\nPreserve list order for `recommended_next_steps`.\nPreserve available fields in each reference item such as `title`, `author`, `year`, and `url`.\n\n## User-facing reply rules\n\n- Group the result into the three modules.\n- Use readable labels instead of raw JSON paths.\n- Do not include low-level execution metadata by default.\n- Mention clearly that the pipeline output is a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n- Append the analyzer image itself when an analyzer image URL is available.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774039802686}}
{"type":"message","id":"2feadbd8","parentId":"8ec8f159","timestamp":"2026-03-20T20:50:07.090Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Inspecting skill directory**\n\nI need to check the skill directory for any existing scripts or templates. It's essential to determine the local CT image, but there isn't a clear path. I should use the newest supported image under inbound. I might not even have a file, so I'll inspect the inbound and skill files and possibly run the script. There seems to be a bit of uncertainty, so I’ll just take it step by step!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0e33da8a38a28db00169bdb2fb86dc819197dba798e1eee53f\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpvbL-KAEvDagDA-Hif2Ncqv3-UELIj44LBmxKpq2-zqR5bx7C_me3yxmqVkRBqxmVdM9m-90uH40sgdBk5I1R1Jtn36E57FDEY0XjCYwKj7MiWSh42NJNDTgJJogmkU77wjF1-CoSZweFVVKDTxbAL2ulpUwbbE7uS9cCdGzL-CzcSEkb05nSmHgAgGzfLw_lKylbEdprypQtjwSCcDNV1lR3Q6tS1X_83-SlKti7B9Rc34-nsKxAO4zdZ0kuuImuzyqMolDovurX5ogL5nmLmDjf_X276L3l10RTdElP1AdcNJTzEOxfQcrqIiVwEmgnAySBUak0Px39jx1hBpUFJYJcBitEJDGHWdmeVQd9nFm0qDJW9MNh92JSpF5wpoXFmn3f7kYkUfbjdnkpxgeupkhi_RifHXfU-UC6373yztnQK1oggtQV_MaAgfHWH7wDqP1b1rf10TNTNA_c1Pi9cGYaAYJQisA2a3J5ROdIsyk7ff3gTEQfZdqYX9zgR8_L_gmyUKnNuZpqhnbUSGDZx0esOKNmLJ7Y8C7vHZFquI96psnWevZA3VqjzxuePPHp9Gb94VfiAhk2m44bEne7DvCRkz3I4rszqAQeTtvA3VPGKQVRjFab5c4pKwqhLReY4vSOcmbN2euQjhKDeacspBbtSp7ARAlmADdLL4i0pIXorn0qXO8Uy1qSJgfa_a01RRBBcNv7cenj1Zpigp80y740HjJUdDYXfFV_w6Eq2tfzt2NshaiBYEfVqaWBEIdGAAdhTuiQH_YrnEo7HjQ18zuOqCU3xDRvIDqCf7vX2YOlfzaz2AGW5sW1slDvk5jDlPRGyTYxfeXqkFpdGt_U_qS_t5Pd7saL88vCaCk0VDKt4DLY_FyUSulPIHy_cGLkN3ynd7sh6yP3hlvOvTuBvdCBc00DY0PVxktuC7hA5tF7g0PAa2N2fsxenUh81_KGtsN6SpcIUaV6i2mwj71VUjnohOwyQtfovfRrZIQcsC-qm4UqwjDmDu6RjWc6VNIup721BTXdlLW47hRINEpDE3EgdPMudJnN5Hfew_yx4UC1dTnBjrb6SDII-WjvQnb8PAqZVq3eaDtT6BzW6iDW6UyNRYfph1Lhc6kEJ4MoeFaTlMcxl0D7M-3FIoQ_Z_pPvIIId8rrdtlTN-jBvlfjcNPQ7Q==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Inspecting skill directory**\\n\\nI need to check the skill directory for any existing scripts or templates. It's essential to determine the local CT image, but there isn't a clear path. I should use the newest supported image under inbound. I might not even have a file, so I'll inspect the inbound and skill files and possibly run the script. There seems to be a bit of uncertainty, so I’ll just take it step by step!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"I’ll use the most recent inbound image if you didn’t mean a specific path, and I’ll save all four artifacts in the workspace as requested.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e33da8a38a28db00169bdb2fece4c81918464eea5172bdabd\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_tkNwmO7tGyZo6qHTTmoXGfhz|fc_0e33da8a38a28db00169bdb2fedcd08191988ec61296428156","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id 495506013","workdir":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace","yieldMs":10000,"timeout":120},"partialJson":"{\"command\":\"python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/kidney-pipeline-execution/scripts/pipeline_execution_tool.py --telegram-user-id 495506013\",\"workdir\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\",\"yieldMs\":10000,\"timeout\":120}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1118,"output":157,"cacheRead":8832,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":10107,"cost":{"input":0.002795,"output":0.002355,"cacheRead":0.002208,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.007358}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774039802688}}
